lisa-design:
- Tag selection reuses release.ComponentTag (strict [<component>-]vX.Y.Z[-pre]) instead of a new parser, so v0, v0.1, latest are rejected the same way the release workflows reject them.
- Tags are additionally matched by VERSION against r.Versions (what the release PR proposed), not by component name: the train doesn't know release-please's component names (package-name/component config), and the root package may use include-component-in-tag. Empty Versions falls back to strict parsing only.
- The filter is applied once, before r.Tags is stored, so finish() no longer asks for a GitHub release of a floating tag (which has none) either.
- Change kept local to publish() + a new publish_test.go to avoid conflicts with parallel internal/train PRs (#64).

